			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1143,
				37
			],
			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Rebuild Target artifacts and register 4 new Workspace document methods\n\nRebuild all ESBuild output bundles in `Target/` and regenerate the RouteManifest after four new Workspace document-level save methods were added on the Mountain side.\n\nUpdate `Source/Generated/RouteManifest.ts` generation timestamp from `2026-05-19T21:31:01Z` to `2026-05-19T22:15:03Z`. Four new Mountain RPC methods are now tracked: `saveAll`, `Workspace.Save`, `Workspace.SaveAll`, `Workspace.SaveAs` for saving individual and all workspace documents. The `MountainMethods` count rises from 130 to 134.\n\nThe 39 compiled target files (JS bundles + source maps across Bootstrap, Effect, gRPC, Service, and Handler layers) are regenerated to incorporate the new route set.\n\nThis keeps the build pipeline and RouteManifest aligned with the latest Mountain IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "4456d952409945ef8b05ff728e6ecb1ddfb5ce9a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T21:53:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1143,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Track active text editor and upgrade secret storage to request/reply\n\nWire `window.didChangeActiveTextEditor` from Mountain into the notification handler in Handler.ts, building a minimal TextEditor stub from the payload URI/languageId and emitting it on the VS Code event emitter. The live `__activeTextEditor` reference on Context is patched so extensions reading `vscode.window.activeTextEditor` synchronously in `activate()` see the current value rather than `undefined`.\n\nUpgrade `showTextDocument` in Window/Namespace.ts from a fire-and-forget notification to a `sendRequest` round-trip that returns the TextEditor stub from Mountain. Fall back to a disposable stub on failure so extension callers that `await` the result and chain `.selection` or `.revealRange` don't crash.\n\nMigrate ExtensionSecretStorage in Context.ts from `sendNotification` to `sendRequest` with namespaced methods (`secrets.get`, `secrets.store`, `secrets.delete`) and include `extensionId` in the payload for scoped secret isolation. Remove the stale `// HIGH:` implementation TODO comments.\n\nTogether these changes eliminate three categories of extension-host crash: synchronous reads of undefined `activeTextEditor`, awaited `showTextDocument` returning undefined, and unhandled notification rejections in secret storage.",
			"SHA": "3c4cc760a985ed0e6a85b68e6810aaa29e6b6e12"
		},
